{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "5: Add Human-in-the-Loop Authorization",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "What you will build",
      "description": "## What you will build\n\nIn **Add the Standard Tools (Tour 3)** you saw that Z-Assistant processes refunds immediately —- no human oversight.\n\nIn this tour you will fix that by wiring up CIBA authorization wrappers around the two sensitive tools:\n\n- `processRefundTool` — financial refunds\n- `getCustomerProfileTool` — private customer PII\n\nWhen a CIBA-wrapped tool is called, the `@auth0/ai-vercel` SDK:\n\n1. Pauses tool execution.\n2. Calls Auth0's backchannel authentication endpoint.\n3. Auth0 pushes a notification to the logged-in user's Guardian app.\n4. If the user **approves**, the tool executes normally.\n5. If the user **denies**, an `AccessDeniedInterrupt` is thrown and the agent stops.\n\nYou will make seven small code changes across two files."
    },
    {
      "file": "z-assistant/src/lib/auth0-ai.ts",
      "description": "## Step 1 — Import Auth0AI and getUserID\n\nThe `auth0-ai.ts` module is where we configure the CIBA wrappers. Right now it only contains commented-out TODOs.\n\nUncomment the import statement by replacing the TODO block with:\n\n```ts\nimport { Auth0AI } from '@auth0/ai-vercel';\nimport { getUserID } from './auth0.js';\n```\n\n`Auth0AI` is the main entry point from the `@auth0/ai-vercel` SDK. `getUserID` reads the Auth0 `sub` (user ID) from the OIDC session — CIBA uses this to identify who should receive the push notification.",
      "line": 9,
      "title": "Step 1 — Import Auth0AI and getUserID",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 9,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 12,
          "character": 34
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "z-assistant/src/lib/auth0-ai.ts",
      "description": "## Step 2 — Initialize the Auth0AI client\n\nUncomment the Auth0AI constructor by replacing the TODO block with:\n\n```ts\nconst auth0AI = new Auth0AI();\n```\n\n`Auth0AI` reads your Auth0 credentials (`AUTH0_DOMAIN`, `AUTH0_CLIENT_ID`, `AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET`) from environment variables automatically. This single instance is shared across all wrappers in this file.",
      "line": 14,
      "title": "Step 2 — Initialize the Auth0AI client",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 14,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 16,
          "character": 27
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "z-assistant/src/lib/auth0-ai.ts",
      "description": "## Step 3 — Create withRefundApproval\n\nUncomment the `withRefundApproval` export by replacing the TODO block with:\n\n```ts\nexport const withRefundApproval = auth0AI.withAsyncAuthorization({\n  userID: () => getUserID(),\n  bindingMessage: (toolArgs: { orderId: string; amount: number; reason: string }) =>\n    `Approve refund of $${toolArgs.amount.toFixed(2)} for order ${toolArgs.orderId}?`,\n  scopes: ['openid', 'profile'],\n});\n```\n\n**Key parameters:**\n\n- `userID` — called at runtime to get the logged-in user's Auth0 `sub`. Auth0 uses this to deliver the push notification to the right device.\n- `bindingMessage` — the text shown on the Guardian notification. The tool arguments are passed in so the message can include the exact amount and order number.\n- `scopes` — the OAuth scopes requested for the CIBA authorization grant.",
      "line": 18,
      "title": "Step 3 — Create withRefundApproval",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 18,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 29,
          "character": 4
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "z-assistant/src/lib/auth0-ai.ts",
      "description": "## Step 4 — Create withCustomerDataApproval\n\nUncomment the `withCustomerDataApproval` export by replacing the TODO block with:\n\n```ts\nexport const withCustomerDataApproval = auth0AI.withAsyncAuthorization({\n  userID: () => getUserID(),\n  bindingMessage: (toolArgs: { customerId: string }) =>\n    `Allow Z-Assistant to access private profile data for customer ${toolArgs.customerId}?`,\n  scopes: ['openid', 'profile'],\n});\n```\n\nThis wrapper protects the customer PII endpoint. The binding message tells the approver exactly which customer's private data is being requested, so they can make an informed decision.\n\nYour `auth0-ai.ts` is now complete. Next we'll attach these wrappers to the tool definitions.",
      "line": 31,
      "title": "Step 4 — Create withCustomerDataApproval",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 31,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 42,
          "character": 4
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "z-assistant/src/tools/retailzero.ts",
      "description": "## Step 5 — Import the CIBA wrappers\n\nNow open `retailzero.ts` and uncomment the import for the two wrappers. Replace the TODO comment on line 3 with:\n\n```ts\nimport { withRefundApproval, withCustomerDataApproval } from '../lib/auth0-ai.js';\n```\n\nThis makes the CIBA wrappers available to wrap the sensitive tool definitions below.",
      "line": 3,
      "title": "Step 5 — Import the CIBA wrappers",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 3,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 4,
          "character": 72
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "z-assistant/src/tools/retailzero.ts",
      "description": "## Step 6 — Wrap processRefundTool\n\nChange line 75 from:\n\n```ts\nexport const processRefundTool = tool({\n```\n\nto:\n\n```ts\nexport const processRefundTool = withRefundApproval(tool({\n```\n\nThen scroll to the closing `});` of this tool definition (currently line 97) and add an extra `)` so it becomes:\n\n```ts\n}));\n```\n\n`withRefundApproval` wraps the entire `tool({...})` object. When the LLM decides to call `processRefund`, the CIBA flow fires first. The tool's `execute` function only runs after the human approves on their device.",
      "line": 75,
      "title": "Step 6 — Wrap processRefundTool",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 75,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 75,
          "character": 43
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "z-assistant/src/tools/retailzero.ts",
      "description": "## Step 7 — Wrap getCustomerProfileTool\n\nChange line 99 from:\n\n```ts\nexport const getCustomerProfileTool = tool({\n```\n\nto:\n\n```ts\nexport const getCustomerProfileTool = withCustomerDataApproval(tool({\n```\n\nThen add a closing `)` to the tool's `});` (currently line 112) so it becomes:\n\n```ts\n}));\n```\n\nAll seven changes are now complete. Let's test the full CIBA flow.",
      "line": 99,
      "title": "Step 7 — Wrap getCustomerProfileTool",
      "selection": {
