    {
      "title": "Test the CIBA flow",
      "description": "## Test the CIBA flow\n\n1. Make sure the **RetailZero API** is running on port 3001. If not:\n   ```\n   cd retailzero-api && npm run dev\n   ```\n\n2. [Start Z-Assistant](command:workbench.action.debug.start) and open it in the browser.\n\n3. Send this prompt:\n   > _\"Process a refund of $216.99 for order ORD-1001, reason: customer not satisfied.\"_\n\n4. Z-Assistant will pause and the **approval banner** will appear at the top of the chat UI.\n\n5. Check your phone — you should see a **Guardian push notification**:\n   > _\"Approve refund of $216.99 for order ORD-1001?\"_\n\n6. **Tap Approve** on your phone.\n\n7. Back in the browser, select **Retry** in the approval banner.\n\n8. Z-Assistant resumes and completes the refund.\n\n---\n\n**Also test denial:**\n\n9. Ask for another refund and tap **Deny** on Guardian instead.\n10. Z-Assistant should respond that the authorization was denied and the refund was not processed.\n\n---\n\n**Congratulations!** Z-Assistant now enforces human-in-the-loop authorization for all sensitive operations. Financial refunds and customer PII access can no longer be executed autonomously — every request requires explicit approval from the authenticated user on their registered device."
    }
  ]
